The {{M2|Aeonglass}} is a {{2|Bosses|Boss}} found in {{2|Glory}}. 

==Pattern==
{{Intents Table/start|Aeonglass}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Ebb
|Intent = Attack4, Defend
|Effect = Deals (22;{{Asc2|9|26}}) damage. Gains 33 {{KW2|Block}}.}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Eye Lasers
|Intent = Attack4
|Effect = Deals (11;{{Asc2|9|12}}) damage x2.}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Increasing Intensity
|Intent = StatusCard, Buff
|Effect = Shuffles (1;{{Asc2|9|2}}) {{C2|Wither|Wither+X}} into your discard pile. Gains (2;{{Asc2|9|3}}) + X {{BD2|Strength}}. Upgrade all {{C2|Wither|Withers}}. {{BD2|Withering Presence}} effect now creates {{C2|Wither|Withers + X}}.}}
{{Intents Table/end}}
'''The Aeonglass''' follows a repeating cycle:
# {{Int|Aeonglass|Ebb||2}}
# {{Int|Aeonglass|Eye Lasers||2}}
# {{Int|Aeonglass|Increasing Intensity||2}}
X equals the amount of times {{Int|Aeonglass|Increasing Intensity||2}} has been used.

==Useful Cards==

* Cards like {{C2|Stoke}}, {{C2|GUARDS!!!}} or {{C2|Flak Cannon}} can efficiently remove multiple copies of Wither from the deck while also providing various other benefits.
* Discarding Withers with cards like {{C2|Prepared}} prevents them from dealing damage this turn, but this means that those Withers will still be present on the next shuffle.
* {{C2|Purity}} can exhaust up to 3(5) copies of Wither and is available to any character, but can only be used once and provides no additional benefits when played.

