== Pattern ==
{{Intents Table/start|Thieving Hopper}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Thievery
|Intent = Attack3, CardDebuff
|Effect = Deals (17;{{Asc2|9|19}}) damage. Steals a card from your deck.}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Flutter
|Intent = Buff
|Effect = Gains {{BD2|Flutter}} (takes 50% less Attack damage, must be hit 5 times to {{BD2|Stun}} it).}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Hat Trick
|Intent = Attack4
|Effect = Deals (21;{{Asc2|9|23}}) damage.}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Nab
|Intent = Attack3
|Effect = Deals (14;{{Asc2|9|16}}) damage.}}
{{Intents Table/row
|Name   = Escape
|Intent = Escape
|Effect = Flees the combat, taking any stolen cards with it.}}
{{Intents Table/end}}
The Thieving Hopper follows a fixed sequence:
* {{Int|Thieving Hopper|Thievery||2}} (stealing a card and dealing damage)
* {{Int|Thieving Hopper|Flutter||2}} (gaining damage reduction)
* {{Int|Thieving Hopper|Hat Trick||2}}
* {{Int|Thieving Hopper|Nab||2}}
* {{Int|Thieving Hopper|Escape||2}} (fleeing the fight permanently)

If it escapes, any cards it stole are lost for the rest of the run. Killing it before it escapes returns the stolen cards.

== Notes ==
* The card stolen by Swipe follows a set order of priority:

1. Non-{{KW2|Imbued}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon|2}} cards

2. Non-{{KW2|Imbued}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare|2}}, {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common|2}}, and {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Event|Event|2}} cards

3. Non-{{KW2|Imbued}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic|2}} and {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Quest|Quest|2}} cards

4. {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Ancient|Ancient|2}} cards or cards that are {{KW2|Imbued}}

5. {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Curse|Curse|2}} cards

* Only cards currently in the player's draw or discard pile when the move is used will be selected. This means under the right circumstances the move can be utilized to remove {{KW2|Eternal}} cards from the player's deck.
* The returned card can be skipped, which means it is possible to defeat the Thieving Hopper, receive all the usual combat rewards and still have a card removed if it is so desired.
* When choosing to take back the stolen card, all the usual interactions on adding a card to the deck apply (e.g. {{R2|Bing Bong}}, or {{R2|Lucky Fysh}}).
* {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Token|Token|2}} cards and {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Status|Status|2}} cards can never be stolen as this would result in being able to add a temporary card into your deck permanently. This also applies to other temporary cards, such as those created by potions.

